#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133563 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca46ab2-488a-5596-b96b-559463731556" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Images of the Standard Basis Vectors Under a Given Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "4748324b-8edf-5fba-90e1-90683887d463" :question/math-academy-id "e-5436" :question/problem "The linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ has the standard matrix \n![](images/34/343c9e46cf59cf4372a563c80dd9010bcece8c04f8babdb95d57c04cdf4a2503.png) \nWhat are the images of the standard basis vectors $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ under the action of $\\mathbf T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ are the first and second columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot\\mathbf{i}$ and $T\\cdot\\mathbf{j}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133564 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2845913-5c76-57f5-a4d3-139a6513225b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "0db64243-ffa4-595b-8555-5ee369450557" :question/math-academy-id "e-5437" :question/problem "In the diagram below, $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf j$ are the vectors of the standard basis of $\\mathbb{R}^2$, while $\\mathbf{i'}$ and $\\mathbf{j'}$ are their images under the linear transformation $\\mathbf T.$\nWhat is the standard matrix of $\\mathbf T?$\n\n![](images/4d/4d1b9e56c0c6214d949d12f45fe4aecea5516971203724ecf573a2b17c6e959a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nFrom the diagram we see that\n\n- the image of $\\mathbf{i}$ is ![](images/cc/ccf1d5e4e5f040782f606fcccc9e183d92a640d4b5148602ce54b3e75ed116a5.png) and\n\n- the image of $\\mathbf{j}$ is ![](images/77/7746aad7a72ef32c38d2851200542f13c7ca8c2c805580b2cee4f78bbd1d0bed.png)\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n![](images/0d/0dfa1b41bac9f0d8250950b3fc538799b1f94271793aef7c13f3f7ce6aaf53ea.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133565 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b057dd5e-f80e-5d3f-84ae-b6aebd5800ea" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Image of the Standard Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "ae7884f7-abb9-56ba-b685-f0eab27ff795" :question/math-academy-id "e-5438" :question/problem "Given that $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j}, \\mathbf k\\}$ is the standard basis of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ and the images of $\\mathbf{i},$ $\\mathbf{j},$ and $\\mathbf{k}$ under the action of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ are\n$\\langle 3, 5, -1 \\rangle,$ $\\langle 0, 4,3 \\rangle,$ and $\\langle -1, 5, -2\\rangle,$ respectively, what is the standard matrix of $\\mathbf{T}?$" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in $\\mathbb{R}^3$ can be represented as a $3\\times 3$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $\\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j},$ and $\\mathbf k$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n![](images/7a/7a94c68b63e914bc3bbc64fb22bfe85ad60746bd2f35cd1dce877f979067c39a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2845913-5c76-57f5-a4d3-139a6513225b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fe14844-7010-584e-bc12-7ff1affe5e07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132596} {:answer/id #uuid "b851afdf-649c-577f-b7d2-f6adc2cf88e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132597} {:answer/id #uuid "163f5f3b-4313-5bb4-86c0-33f8c89b91d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132598} {:answer/id #uuid "1ba61b85-abbf-5833-b6c9-f53612aa0f14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132599} {:answer/id #uuid "7549a231-96e8-503d-a3f9-06c37322af20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132600}] :answer-field/id #uuid "384786b2-da5d-5687-8efa-cabf3fb09792" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132595}] :question/id #uuid "d45923a4-c5c5-54fb-9905-415ac3f45f69" :question/math-academy-id "q-43837" :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad1f032fd5b99252d348d0cf71308ef1de0f65f06ddd9070b569cff69bc506f9.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $i$ and $j$ are the vectors of the standard basis of $R^{2}$, while $i^{′}$ and $j^{′}$ are their images under the linear transformation $T$.\nWhat is the standard matrix of $T$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b057dd5e-f80e-5d3f-84ae-b6aebd5800ea" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Image of the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99606574-1fb7-59fd-8268-8345f0d146ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132602} {:answer/id #uuid "dd257ac9-ba37-5094-abb6-9bf433f92fe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132603} {:answer/id #uuid "3a9abe70-d8b9-5478-8813-0ccdf157c442" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132604} {:answer/id #uuid "5200d9db-0053-5a03-b83e-2967311eac1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132605} {:answer/id #uuid "62d6c06e-86d7-5c84-b618-5057718f5d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132606}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f21fd698-d395-5261-9510-d4e39ef13f4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132601}] :question/id #uuid "7a53abc5-75df-59d0-bf69-6e7c50f35689" :question/math-academy-id "q-43889" :question/problem "Given that ${i, j, k}$ is the standard basis of $R^{3}$ and that the images of $i$, $j$, and $k$ under the action of a linear transformation $T$ are $⟨2,-1, 6⟩$, $⟨7, 2, 0⟩$, and $⟨1,-4, 6⟩$, respectively, what is the standard matrix of $T$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134428 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca46ab2-488a-5596-b96b-559463731556" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Images of the Standard Basis Vectors Under a Given Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f5f35f2-817f-5140-aab1-b1e5cbd185af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$,\nand $\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132608} {:answer/id #uuid "d99804d8-20c0-5413-aa9f-953f8d200d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$,\nand $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132609} {:answer/id #uuid "4faf60bb-11aa-5d65-83db-96a4f83f5d1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$,\nand $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132610} {:answer/id #uuid "75c39589-4a07-5475-8713-cf0668fe73c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$,\nand $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132611} {:answer/id #uuid "7c667266-61db-5c34-8232-7c4e5496fc11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$,\nand $\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132612}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a9fba76a-fa1f-56f3-a156-563fef2e304a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132607}] :question/id #uuid "34b068e8-ab54-5792-afa1-011595ad4802" :question/math-academy-id "q-43890" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$.\nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors ${i, j, k}$ of $R^{3}$ under the action of $T$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134429 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b057dd5e-f80e-5d3f-84ae-b6aebd5800ea" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Image of the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b67713a2-2c9f-51e5-93b8-d5a4e14d754e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132614} {:answer/id #uuid "b77d6421-75eb-5c4e-8fd1-541c69e4bdd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132615} {:answer/id #uuid "c04ffbb9-c047-57