 matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nFrom the diagram we see that \n${i}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ \nand \n${j}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2845913-5c76-57f5-a4d3-139a6513225b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2224cf00-9c61-5f7e-a20e-4ab49991b1e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393781} {:answer/id #uuid "2b556ff2-c047-5a8d-b5df-fba08c731fff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393782} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe4d06b-075d-5500-939c-2f85de0b2408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393783} {:answer/id #uuid "45511535-805a-572f-815c-c4e9c6822f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393784} {:answer/id #uuid "c4ab4fcc-b4a1-51c6-ab50-8695e294ec6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b556ff2-c047-5a8d-b5df-fba08c731fff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393782} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ea2f22b-54cb-5f9a-9611-f131357399a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5ff535c-ef1d-5a3b-a208-109a9dfed530" :question/math-academy-id "q-77999" :question/problem "![](images/09/09423b097ab02b339f15af831e0e35f59ff88cb00c0ef72d3693ce9f24e6b9dc.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $i$ and $j$ are the vectors of the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$, while ${i}^{′}$ and ${j}^{′}$ are their images under the linear transformation $T.$\nWhat is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nFrom the diagram we see that \n${i}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ \nand \n${j}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}]}
